WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.467
A long time ago, many beavers lived in Scotland.

2
00:00:09.468 --> 00:00:16.312
But their fur became very popular for making coats, and people thought beavers tasted delicious.

3
00:00:16.313 --> 00:00:19.530
They hunted all the beavers until they were gone.

4
00:00:19.531 --> 00:00:23.012
That happened over four hundred years ago.

5
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:27.865
Today scientists are worried that the beavers have not returned.

6
00:00:27.866 --> 00:00:31.431
So they have decided to learn more about the beaver's habitat.

7
00:00:31.432 --> 00:00:34.861
Habitat means the natural place where an animal lives.

8
00:00:34.862 --> 00:00:41.416
If scientists know more about how beavers live, they can encourage beavers to return to Scotland.

9
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:48.121
When a beaver turns three years old, it leaves its family and swims downriver to build a new home.

10
00:00:48.122 --> 00:00:50.978
A beaver's home is called a lodge.

11
00:00:50.979 --> 00:00:56.699
It looks like a big pile of sticks, but it is actually a carefully designed house.

12
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:03.667
Beaver lodges are made of small tree branches and mud that are piled in the shape of an upside down bowl.

13
00:01:03.668 --> 00:01:10.413
Most lodges are two to three meters high, three to six meters wide, and full of tunnels.

14
00:01:10.414 --> 00:01:14.158
Some tunnels lead to the rooms inside where the beavers live.

15
00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:16.217
Other tunnels store food.

16
00:01:16.218 --> 00:01:22.909
There are also secret tunnels that confuse predators—so hungry animals don't make beaver soup for dinner!

17
00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:29.862
Beavers build their lodges in streams, and the entrance is always underwater so that it is hard to find.

18
00:01:29.863 --> 00:01:34.453
For a long time, scientists were confused about the size of a beaver lodge.

19
00:01:34.454 --> 00:01:40.873
Most beaver families have a mom, a dad, and one to four babies, which are called kits.

20
00:01:40.874 --> 00:01:43.503
Why did they need so much room?

21
00:01:43.504 --> 00:01:49.921
After watching beavers for a long time, scientists found two answers to their question.

22
00:01:49.922 --> 00:01:56.320
First, beavers build big homes because they need thick walls to keep out predators.

23
00:01:56.321 --> 00:02:00.013
Second, beavers need a place to store their food.

24
00:02:00.014 --> 00:02:08.222
Since beavers do not hibernate, they need a warm, safe place and lots of food when the weather gets cold.

25
00:02:08.223 --> 00:02:12.131
In the north many lakes turn to ice in the winter.

26
00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:21.451
The ice often traps beavers inside their lodge, so beavers need to store enough food to make sure they don't get hungry.

27
00:02:21.452 --> 00:02:29.902
Beavers will often build their lodge with young trees on the inside so they can eat the bark during winter.

28
00:02:29.903 --> 00:02:34.904
Beavers love to eat bark, especially from aspen and cottonwood trees.

29
00:02:34.905 --> 00:02:41.200
Beavers also like to eat clover and raspberry bushes, but their favorite food is water lilies.

30
00:02:41.201 --> 00:02:45.903
Many people think beavers eat fish, but this is not true.

31
00:02:45.904 --> 00:02:50.576
The best way to find a beaver habitat is to look for a lot of water.

32
00:02:50.577 --> 00:02:53.686
Beavers always build a dam near their lodge.

33
00:02:53.687 --> 00:02:56.972
It makes the stream slow down and creates a pond.

34
00:02:56.973 --> 00:03:03.669
This way the lodge is surrounded by water, making it look like a tiny island.

35
00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:10.369
After watching beavers for a long time, scientists learned that beavers live for about ten years.

36
00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:15.053
Once two beavers decide to make a family, they never leave each other.

37
00:03:15.054 --> 00:03:20.482
Beavers somehow always know when there are too many beavers living on their river.

38
00:03:20.483 --> 00:03:24.980
They have the right-sized family to keep the river from getting crowded.

39
00:03:24.981 --> 00:03:29.648
Now that the scientists know what beavers like to eat, where they like to live,

40
00:03:29.649 --> 00:03:37.929
and how they build their homes, they are working to make Scotland a place that beavers can call home.
